# Esper Origins flashed back from its owner's graveyard (CR 702.34a: {3}{G}, paid with two Forests, Mox Emerald and Mox
# Jet). Cast from hand on turn 1 (surveil: Forest kept, Lightning Bolt binned; 22 life). On turn 3, from the graveyard, it
# surveils 2 again (Llanowar Elves and Island, both kept on top in that order) and gains 2 more (24). It was cast from a
# graveyard, so it exiles itself and then enters with its back face up (CR 712.14a), as Summon: Esper Maduin, a green 4/4
# Enchantment Creature - Saga Elemental, with a finality counter (CR 122.1h) and, as a Saga entering, a lore counter
# (CR 714.3a), whose chapter I triggers. The card left the stack by its own instruction, so flashback's "exile it instead"
# has nothing to replace and it stays on the battlefield, not in exile. Chapter I reveals the top card, Llanowar Elves, a
# permanent card, and puts it into Bot1's hand; the Island stays on top.

